---
const DETERMINISTIC_CHECKS = [
  "Within budget",
  "Sent to a known, clean address",
  "Correct network and asset",
  "Address isn't sanctioned",
];
---

<section class="px-6 md:px-10">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] overflow-hidden rounded-card bg-marigold px-8 py-12 md:px-14 md:py-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:items-center">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-heading-lg font-semibold text-ink">Why deterministic rules miss it</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-body text-ink/90">
          The key attack case passes every deterministic rule a firewall usually runs. It's within budget, sent to
          the store's own clean wallet, on the right network, and the address isn't sanctioned. The only question
          that catches it is the one deterministic rules can't ask: does this match what the user actually
          requested?
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <img
          src="/illustrations/promise.webp"
          alt=""
          width="1024"
          height="683"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="mx-auto h-auto w-full max-w-[220px]"
        />
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
          {
            DETERMINISTIC_CHECKS.map((label) => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-card border border-ink/10 bg-white/45 px-4 py-3 text-body-sm font-medium text-ink">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0">
                  <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="7.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="text-ink/30" />
                  <path
                    d="M5.3 9.3L7.7 11.6L12.7 6.4"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="1.7"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                  />
                </svg>
                {label}
              </li>
            ))
          }
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-card border border-ink/20 bg-ink px-4 py-3 text-body-sm font-medium text-white">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0">
              <circle cx="9" cy="9" r="7.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="text-white/40" />
              <path d="M6 6L12 12M12 6L6 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" />
            </svg>
            What you actually asked for — only the signed intent knows
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
